1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,630
One thing we always remember from our childhood is our favourite teddy bear.
童年里总有一样东西让我们念念不忘，那就是自己最心爱的泰迪熊。

2
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:11,000
This soft, ragged toy was our comfort and companion.
这个柔软破旧的玩具曾是我们的慰藉与伙伴。

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:21,800
As we grow up, we normally give up our childish ways, and our furry friend often ends up in storage or at a jumble sale.
长大后，我们通常会褪去稚气，而这个毛茸茸的小伙伴往往会被收进储物间，或是送去旧货义卖会。

4
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,690
But that’s not the case for everyone.
但并非所有人都是如此。

5
00:00:24,690 --> 00:00:31,110
It seems that some grown-ups continue to need their cuddly toy by their sides.
有些成年人似乎依然需要毛绒玩具陪伴左右。

6
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:37,780
One sleep survey suggested a tenth of people in the UK need a teddy bear in bed.
一项睡眠调查显示，英国有十分之一的人睡觉时必须抱着泰迪熊。

7
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:45,880
And for some adults, soft toys remain an essential presence – they take them wherever they go.
对部分成年人而言，毛绒玩具是生活中不可或缺的存在——他们走到哪儿都会带着。

8
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:53,890
A cuddly toy can come in many forms – animals, strange shapes or just a piece of stuffed material.
毛绒玩具的形态多种多样，有动物造型、奇趣形状，或是一块简单的填充布料。

9
00:00:53,890 --> 00:01:04,950
But it’s the teddy bear in particular that seems to have an enduring appeal – it gives us a nostalgic feeling and a reminder of our younger days.
但唯独泰迪熊似乎拥有经久不衰的吸引力——它能唤起我们的怀旧之情，让我们想起年少时光。

10
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:19,140
Writing for the BBC, historian David Cannadine says, “Perhaps it’s that bears represent the happy security of a childhood friend who never changes or lets you down.”
历史学家大卫·坎纳丁在为BBC撰稿时表示：“或许是因为泰迪熊象征着童年玩伴那种永恒不变、永远不会让你失望的温暖安全感。”

11
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:25,510
For whatever reason, teddies appeal to both children and adults of all ages.
无论出于何种原因，泰迪熊都深受各个年龄段的儿童与成年人的喜爱。

12
00:01:25,510 --> 00:01:35,930
The teddy bear is much celebrated these days, and they’ve become something that we don’t just grow up with – people buy them as adults too.
如今，泰迪熊早已成为备受追捧的存在，它不再只是我们童年的玩伴——成年人也会特意购买。

13
00:01:35,930 --> 00:01:47,130
There are shops which sell only teddy bears, there are teddy bear museums in many countries, and teddy bear festivals regularly take place around the world.
市面上有专门售卖泰迪熊的商店，许多国家建有泰迪熊博物馆，世界各地还会定期举办泰迪熊主题节日。

14
00:01:47,130 --> 00:01:55,360
While our soft toys offer us a kind of comfort blanket, some experts say it’s nothing to be ashamed of.
尽管毛绒玩具就像我们的“心灵慰藉毯”，但一些专家表示，这绝非什么丢人的事。

15
00:01:55,360 --> 00:02:02,210
It’s sometimes good to let go of the constraints of adult life and be a big kid again.
偶尔放下成年人的条条框框，重新做一回“大孩子”，其实是件好事。

16
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:14,920
And research commissioned by Barclaycard in the UK found 44% of adults have purchased playthings they enjoyed as children because they bring back happy memories.
巴克莱卡公司在英国开展的一项研究发现，44%的成年人会购买童年时喜爱的玩具，因为这些玩具能勾起美好的回忆。

17
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:20,190
Colouring books, cuddly toys and board games were top of the list.
填色书、毛绒玩具和桌面游戏高居榜单前列。

18
00:02:20,190 --> 00:02:26,640
So, if you’re still keeping your teddy a secret, don’t worry – you’re not alone!
所以，如果你还在偷偷珍藏着自己的泰迪熊，别担心——你绝对不是个例！
